{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The exploration completed and exposed a state mismatch: before reconnection, all nodes had decided `base=11`; afterward, node 3 reported decided index 2 but returned only `tail=22`. Nodes 1 and 2 retained both keys. The trace shows a genuine delta `AcceptSync` from index 1 to 2. I’ll now fix a check with an explicit content-preservation obligation and correlated input and result events.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))\nprint(json.dumps(s['\"'$defs'\"']['CodeAnchor'],indent=2))\nPY\nnl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/messages.rs | tail -80\nnl -ba ../agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/log.md | head -110\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))\nprint(json.dumps(s['\"'$defs'\"']['CodeAnchor'],indent=2))\nPY\nnl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/messages.rs | tail -80\nnl -ba ../agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/log.md | head -110\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"source_ids\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"boundary_complete\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Boundary Complete\"\n    },\n    \"kind\": {\n      \"default\": \"declaration\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"declaration\",\n        \"interface_member\",\n        \"callsite\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Kind\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"material_id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Material Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"start_line\": {\n      \"minimum\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Start Line\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"end_line\": {\n      \"minimum\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"End Line\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"symbol\": {\n      \"title\": \"Symbol\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"material_id\",\n    \"start_line\",\n    \"end_line\",\n    \"symbol\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"CodeAnchor\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n   267\timpl<T> Message<T>\n   268\twhere\n   269\t    T: Entry,\n   270\t{\n   271\t    /// Get the sender id of the message\n   272\t    pub fn get_sender(&self) -> NodeId {\n   273\t        match self {\n   274\t            Message::SequencePaxos(p) => p.from,\n   275\t            Message::BLE(b) => b.from,\n   276\t            #[cfg(feature = \"async_runtime\")]\n   277\t            Message::AsyncRuntime(a) => a.from,\n   278\t        }\n   279\t    }\n   280\t\n   281\t    /// Get the receiver id of the message\n   282\t    pub fn get_receiver(&self) -> NodeId {\n   283\t        match self {\n   284\t            Message::SequencePaxos(p) => p.to,\n   285\t            Message::BLE(b) => b.to,\n   286\t            #[cfg(feature = \"async_runtime\")]\n   287\t            Message::AsyncRuntime(a) => a.to,\n   288\t        }\n   289\t    }\n   290\t}\n   291\t\n   292\t/// Messages exchanged between actor instances for `append_notify` correlation.\n   293\t/// These do not touch the core Paxos protocol — they run alongside it.\n   294\t#[cfg(feature = \"async_runtime\")]\n   295\tpub mod async_runtime {\n   296\t    use crate::{ballot_leader_election::Ballot, storage::Entry, util::NodeId};\n   297\t    #[cfg(feature = \"serde\")]\n   298\t    use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n   299\t\n   300\t    /// A unique identifier for a tagged proposal, used to correlate a\n   301\t    /// forwarded entry with its assigned log index.\n   302\t    #[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug, Eq, PartialEq, Hash)]\n   303\t    #[cfg_attr(feature = \"serde\", derive(Serialize, Deserialize))]\n   304\t    pub struct EntryId(pub uuid::Uuid);\n   305\t\n   306\t    /// Wrapper carrying sender/receiver for an [`AsyncRuntimeMsg`].\n   307\t    #[derive(Clone, Debug)]\n   308\t    #[cfg_attr(feature = \"serde\", derive(Serialize, Deserialize))]\n   309\t    pub struct AsyncRuntimeMessage<T>\n   310\t    where\n   311\t        T: Entry,\n   312\t    {\n   313\t        /// Sender of `msg`.\n   314\t        pub from: NodeId,\n   315\t        /// Receiver of `msg`.\n   316\t        pub to: NodeId,\n   317\t        /// The runtime-message content.\n   318\t        pub msg: AsyncRuntimeMsg<T>,\n   319\t    }\n   320\t\n   321\t    /// Runtime-layer messages used by the actor to correlate `append_notify` calls\n   322\t    /// with the log index the leader eventually assigns.\n   323\t    #[allow(missing_docs)]\n   324\t    #[derive(Clone, Debug)]\n   325\t    #[cfg_attr(feature = \"serde\", derive(Serialize, Deserialize))]\n   326\t    pub enum AsyncRuntimeMsg<T>\n   327\t    where\n   328\t        T: Entry,\n   329\t    {\n   330\t        /// Follower actor → leader actor. Carries entries the originator(s) want\n   331\t        /// tracked, batched into one message. Replaces the untagged\n   332\t        /// `PaxosMsg::ProposalForward` path when the caller used `append_notify`.\n   333\t        TaggedProposal { entries: Vec<(EntryId, T)> },\n   334\t        /// Leader actor → originating follower actor. Carries, for each entry in a\n   335\t        /// previously received `TaggedProposal` batch that was actually accepted,\n   336\t        /// the log index the leader assigned, plus the single full ballot under\n   337\t        /// which the *whole batch* was accepted (one ballot, not per-entry: the\n   338\t        /// leader processes one incoming `TaggedProposal` synchronously with no\n   339\t        /// yield points, so every entry in it is necessarily accepted under the\n   340\t        /// same ballot).\n   341\t        Assigned {\n   342\t            ballot: Ballot,\n   343\t            entries: Vec<(EntryId, usize)>,\n   344\t        },\n   345\t    }\n   346\t}\n     1\tWe now show how to read and write the replicated log. The replicated log is *append-only*. To append an entry we call the following:\n     2\t\n     3\t```rust\n     4\tlet write_entry = KeyValue { key: String::from(\"a\"), value: 123 };\n     5\tomni_paxos.append(write_entry).expect(\"Failed to append\");\n     6\t```\n     7\t\n     8\tThis will cause our `write_entry` to be proposed to get decided in the replicated log. Appends can be pipelined without waiting for preceding entries to be decided. Furthermore, `append()` can be called on any node. If the calling node is not the leader, the entry will be forwarded. \n     9\t\n    10\t## Reading the Log\n    11\tReads are also handled by calling various functions on `OmniPaxos`. To read the entry at a specific index `idx` of the log we call `omni_paxos.read_entry(idx)`. We can also read a specific range of log entries with `omni_paxos.read_entries()`. \n    12\t\n    13\t```rust\n    14\t/*** Read a single entry ***/\n    15\tlet idx = 5;\n    16\tlet read_entry = omni_paxos.read(idx);\n    17\t\n    18\t/*** Read a range ***/\n    19\tlet read_entries = omni_paxos.read_entries(2..5);\n    20\t``` \n    21\t\n    22\tThe read functions return `Option<LogEntry>` and `Option<Vec<LogEntry>>` respectively, where `None` is returned if the index or range is out of bounds. `LogEntry` is an enum with the following variants:\n    23\t- `Decided(T)`: The entry is decided and guaranteed to not be reverted. It is thus safe to apply a decided entry to the application state. For instance, in our case, it is safe to update our key-value store when we read a `Decided(KeyValue)` entry.\n    24\t- `Undecided(T)`: The entry is NOT decided and might be removed from the log at a later time. However, it could be useful in applications that allow speculative execution for example.\n    25\t- `Trimmed(TrimmedIndex)`: We tried to read an index where the entry has already been trimmed. \n    26\t- `Snapshotted(SnapshottedEntry<T>)`: The index we read has already been compacted into a snapshot. We can access the snapshot from the field `snapshot` in `SnapshottedEntry`. In our case our this will correspond to `KVSnapshot` that we defined [here](../compaction).\n    27\t- `StopSign(StopSign)`: This Sequence Paxos instance has been stopped for reconfiguration. This implies that this log will not be appended anymore and one should use the new Sequence Paxos instead for writing.\n    28\t\n    29\tIt is also possible to only read decided entries or snapshot from a specific index using `read_decided_suffix(idx)`.\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\np=open('delta_explore.rs').read().replace('storage::{Entry, Snapshot}', 'storage::{Entry, Snapshot, SnapshotType}')\np=p.replace('fn explore_delta_reconnect()', 'fn check_delta_reconnect()')\np=p.replace('            if let Message::SequencePaxos(p) = &msg {','            let mut selected_sync = None;\\\\n            if let Message::SequencePaxos(p) = &msg {')\nneedle='                    println\"'!(\"CA_EVENT {}\",json!({\"event\":\"sync_input\"'\"'\nstart=p.index(needle);end=p.index('\\\\n',start)\np=p[:start]+'''                    if stage == \\\"reconnect\\\" && to == 3 {\n                        let delta = matches\"'!(&a.log_sync.decided_snapshot, Some(SnapshotType::Delta(_)));\n                        let receiver = observe(&nodes[(to-1) as usize]);\n                        let leader = observe(&nodes[(from-1) as usize]);\n                        let expected = serde_json::to_string(&leader[\"state\"]).unwrap();\n                        println!(\"CA_EVENT {}\",json!({\"event\":\"sync_admitted\",\"case_id\":\"delta_reconnect\",\"receiver\":to,\"leader\":from,\"config\":a.n.config_id,\"round\":a.n.n,\"session\":a.seq_num.session,\"delta\":delta,\"old_decided\":receiver[\"decided\"],\"old_accepted\":receiver[\"accepted\"],\"old_state\":serde_json::to_string(&receiver[\"state\"]).unwrap(),\"leader_decided\":leader[\"decided\"],\"incoming_decided\":a.decided_idx,\"sync_idx\":a.log_sync.sync_idx,\"expected_state\":expected}));\n                        selected_sync = Some((a.n.config_id,a.n.n,a.seq_num.session,a.decided_idx));\n                    }'\"''' +p[end:]\np=p.replace('            nodes[(to-1) as usize].handle_incoming(msg);','''            nodes[(to-1) as usize].handle_incoming(msg);\n            if let Some((config,round,session,incoming_decided)) = selected_sync {\n                let n = &nodes[(to-1) as usize];\n                let observed = observe(n);\n                let completed = n.get_current_leader() == Some((from,true)) && n.get_decided_idx() == incoming_decided && n.get_accepted_idx() >= incoming_decided;\n                println\"'!(\"CA_EVENT {}\",json!({\"event\":\"sync_result\",\"case_id\":\"delta_reconnect\",\"receiver\":to,\"leader\":from,\"config\":config,\"round\":round,\"session\":session,\"completed\":completed,\"decided\":n.get_decided_idx(),\"accepted\":n.get_accepted_idx(),\"compacted\":n.get_compacted_idx(),\"actual_state\":serde_json::to_string(&observed[\"state\"]).unwrap(),\"read\":format!(\"{:?}\",n.read_decided_suffix(0))}));\n            }'\"''')\nopen('delta_check.rs','w').write(p)\nr=json.load(open('../research.json')); q=r['candidates'][0]['question'];q['disposition']='ready_for_check';q['unknowns']=[]\nq['trigger_rationale']+=' Exploration f63fdbb7f34a4c76ba00402d9a313229 reached that history and observed missing prior key after successful sync; fixed fresh execution is now needed.'\nsrc=['S-sync-storage','S-storage-getters','S-sync-producer','S-memory','S-follower-prepare','S-leader-accept','S-api']\nexp=['S-snapshot-doc','S-storage-contract','S-log-contract','S-snapshot-test']\nclaim='C-snapshot-preservation'; bid='bind-sync'\nground=dict(source_ids=src,expectation_ids=exp,binding_ids=[bid],derivation='Snapshot documentation describes compaction without discarding data and key-value create/merge semantics. The Storage SnapshotType contract defines Delta as changes since an earlier snapshot. The log contract guarantees decided entries are not reverted. Therefore after valid synchronization, the snapshot plus decided suffix must represent the same decided key-value prefix as the selected sender history; a delta must preserve earlier keys not overwritten by later entries. Existing snapshot tests independently compare snapshot contents to the input prefix. sync_log and its caller bind that requirement to actual history installation, not just index equality.',applicability='Valid fixed three-node configuration, correct key-value Snapshot implementation, fault-free MemoryStorage, generated FIFO messages with temporary partition and reconnect, no concurrent calls, no log trimming or reconfiguration.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Complete snapshot replacement bypasses the delta merge; not the selected input.'])\nob=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='consensus_safety',description='When a replica successfully installs a delta snapshot through valid synchronization of a decided log prefix, its snapshot and remaining decided entries must preserve the application state represented by that selected prefix, including prior decided keys not overwritten by the delta.',source_ids=src+exp,scope=dict(description='Content preservation of decided key-value state across successful follower delta synchronization.',assumptions=['Snapshot create folds key assignments and merge applies later assignments.','Storage conforms to its interface and calls are serialized.','Messages originate in the implementation and are delivered to intended configured replicas; temporary network disconnection is followed by reconnected notification.'],excluded=['Progress deadlines','Persistent backend crashes','Async runtime notification','Complete snapshot branch','Cross-configuration message routing']),pending=[],grounding=ground)\nbinding=dict(id=bid,material_id='S-sync-storage',symbol='sync_log',start_line=313,end_line=360,description='Installs accepted history and complete/delta snapshot. Delta merge reconstructs local base after setting incoming decided index.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=['S-sync-storage','S-follower-prepare','S-snapshot-doc','S-storage-contract'],rationale='handle_acceptsync synchronously calls this installer before reporting Accepted; its stored snapshot is the decided prefix representation returned by read APIs.')])\ncandidate=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=r['candidates'][0]['id'],question=q,rationale='The documented snapshot semantics and actual public-API exploration establish an applicable content preservation responsibility; retain observed discrepancy pending fixed check and correspondence.',obligation=ob,bindings=[binding])\ndef eq(field,value):return dict(field=field,op='eq',value=value)\nleg=dict(source_ids=src+['S-config','S-clock','S-proposal','S-dispatch','S-transport-doc'],expectation_ids=['S-snapshot-doc','S-storage-contract'],binding_ids=[bid],derivation='Fresh nodes and default MemoryStorage are built through validated public configuration. try_become_leader starts genuine Prepare/Promise/AcceptSync. The queue delivers every generated message FIFO while connected, and drops all messages to/from follower 3 during the simulated partition. One base entry is decided everywhere before partition; a second distinct-key assignment is decided by nodes 1 and 2 while follower 3 retains base. Both endpoints are notified after connection restoration. Reconnect drives genuine PrepareReq/Prepare/Promise/AcceptSync. No manufactured protocol messages or storage seeds are used. The finite synchronous history needs no timer to complete: manual leadership and all relevant callbacks are delivered. There is no claim of bounded progress. Snapshot BTreeMap semantics match documented key-value snapshot. The result is sampled immediately after the real handler returns under exclusive ownership; the rest of the generated messages are then drained and all objects normally dropped.',applicability=ground['applicability'],unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=[])\nplan=dict(description='Reproduce the lagging follower delta-base mismatch with a decided one-entry prefix and one further quorum-decided entry during a partition. Record genuine delta admission and synchronous result for the same message session; compare exact canonical key-value content with sender decided state read before delivery.',claim_id=claim,binding_ids=[bid],harness=dict(kind='rust_test',source='',files={},description='Three public OmniPaxos nodes with documented KV snapshot and MemoryStorage, FIFO generated-message pump and partition/reconnect schedule.',semantic_changes=[],legality=leg,prerequisites=[dict(alias='admit',event='sync_admitted',conditions=[eq('case_id','delta_reconnect'),eq('delta',True),eq('old_decided',1),eq('old_accepted',1),eq('old_state','{\\\"base\\\":11}'),eq('leader_decided',2),eq('incoming_decided',2),eq('sync_idx',2),eq('expected_state','{\\\"base\\\":11,\\\"tail\\\":22}')])]),monitors=[dict(id='M-content',checker_id='snapshot_content',event='sync_result',binding_ids=[bid],grounding=ground,admission_alias='admit')],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='snapshot_content',kind='event_assertion',trigger=eq('completed',True),assertion=dict(field='actual_state',op='eq',reference='admit.expected_state'),identity_fields=['case_id','receiver','leader','config','round','session'],description='Exact canonical key-value map content, not just indexes, matches the sender decided prefix when the selected delta handling has completed.')],uncertainties=['One follower-reconnect history; other snapshot paths and persistence faults remain independent.'])\nfeedback=dict(ref_ids=[r['candidates'][0]['id'],'F-snapshot','B-sync','S-sync-storage','S-memory','f63fdbb7f34a4c76ba00402d9a313229'],answered='Exploration completed with exit 0. All nodes first decided base=11 at index 1. With node 3 disconnected, nodes 1 and 2 decided tail=22 at index 2. Reconnect generated Delta({tail:22}) using follower decided base 1. Follower 3 then reported accepted=decided=compacted=2 but read only {tail:22}; other nodes read {base:11,tail:22}. The legal history and content discriminator are reached. Source explains the loss: incoming boundary 2 is cached before local create_decided_snapshot requests [0,2), which MemoryStorage returns empty because local length is 1; the delta alone is then persisted. This is construction knowledge, not formal E